From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phillip Abbott <phillipa@vivi.io>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] adaptivedemux: never block on the manifest lock when handling
 source errors

The legacy adaptivedemux (hlsdemux under playbin/uridecodebin v2) can
deadlock a whole pipeline, and with it any thread that then calls
gst_element_set_state(), whenever one of its stream sources posts an
HTTP error while the playlist is being refreshed:

  * updates_loop holds MANIFEST_LOCK for the whole of update_manifest,
    which downloads the playlist through the shared libsoup session.
  * souphttpsrc posts HTTP status errors synchronously from that shared
    session thread. The message reaches
    gst_adaptive_demux_handle_message, which takes MANIFEST_LOCK and
    blocks, because updates_loop still holds it.
  * updates_loop's download can never complete: the session thread it
    depends on is the one parked on the lock. The souphttpsrc task it
    is joining (gst_pad_stop_task) waits on the same session thread.
  * The application's PAUSED->READY state change then blocks on
    MANIFEST_LOCK as well (gst_adaptive_demux_change_state:574) and the
    UI thread hangs for good.

Seen on every vivi box running YouTube HLS signage once googlevideo
started answering segment requests with 403 (constant error posts).
Present in 1.20.1 and unchanged in 1.26.11; upstream considers the
legacy element superseded by hlsdemux2 (gstreamer#4651 closed without a
fix), which is not reachable from playbin/uridecodebin v2.

Take the manifest lock with g_rec_mutex_trylock in the ERROR handler.
If it is busy, forward the error unchanged instead of converting it to
a retry. The pipeline errors out and the application restarts the item,
which is what would have happened after MAX_DOWNLOAD_ERROR_COUNT
retries anyway. Waiting a bounded time would not help: whenever the
poster is the shared session thread, the lock holder is waiting on
exactly that thread.

The full 4-thread stacks (debuggerd, symbolized) are in
vivi-gf-3.13-hls-deadlock-10.0.0.190-2026-09-08.md.
---
 .../gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c
index cf2ede64ff..b6bfada6bf 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/gst-libs/gst/adaptivedemux/gstadaptivedemux.c
@@ -144,6 +144,8 @@ GST_DEBUG_CATEGORY (adaptivedemux_debug);
     g_rec_mutex_unlock (GST_MANIFEST_GET_LOCK (d)); \
  } G_STMT_END
 
+#define GST_MANIFEST_TRYLOCK(d) (g_rec_mutex_trylock (GST_MANIFEST_GET_LOCK (d)))
+
 #define GST_API_GET_LOCK(d) (&(GST_ADAPTIVE_DEMUX_CAST(d)->priv->api_lock))
 #define GST_API_LOCK(d)   g_mutex_lock (GST_API_GET_LOCK (d));
 #define GST_API_UNLOCK(d) g_mutex_unlock (GST_API_GET_LOCK (d));
@@ -857,7 +859,30 @@ gst_adaptive_demux_handle_message (GstBin * bin, GstMessage * msg)
       gchar *new_error = NULL;
       const GstStructure *details = NULL;
 
-      GST_MANIFEST_LOCK (demux);
+      /* Never block the thread that posted the error on the manifest lock.
+       *
+       * With a shared libsoup session (the default since 1.20), HTTP errors
+       * from a stream's internal source are posted synchronously from the
+       * session thread that services every souphttpsrc in the pipeline. If
+       * the updates task holds the manifest lock while it downloads the
+       * playlist (it does, for the whole of update_manifest), that download
+       * needs the same session thread, which is now parked here waiting for
+       * the lock. Nothing can ever release it: updates_loop -> session
+       * thread -> manifest lock -> updates_loop. A state change to READY
+       * then blocks on the manifest lock too and the application hangs.
+       *
+       * If the lock is busy, give up on the retry path and forward the error
+       * unchanged. The pipeline errors out and the application restarts it,
+       * which is what would have happened after MAX_DOWNLOAD_ERROR_COUNT
+       * retries anyway. Waiting would not help: the holder needs this thread.
+       */
+      if (!GST_MANIFEST_TRYLOCK (demux)) {
+        GST_WARNING_OBJECT (demux,
+            "manifest lock busy while handling error from %" GST_PTR_FORMAT
+            ", forwarding the error instead of retrying",
+            GST_MESSAGE_SRC (msg));
+        break;
+      }
 
       for (iter = demux->streams; iter; iter = g_list_next (iter)) {
         GstAdaptiveDemuxStream *cur = iter->data;
-- 
2.39.5
